From 9a8b7c6d5e4f3a2b1c0d9e8f7a6b5c4d3e2f1a0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sovereign Systems Engineering <systems@upl-core.org>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 01:48:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [mono][interp] Lazily initialize InterpContext in interp_set_resume_state to prevent WASM AOT exception unwinding abort (#138322)

Fixes #138322.

In multithreaded browser WebAssembly ([browser][mt]), threads executing purely
AOT-compiled code do not initialize a thread-local interpreter context (`InterpContext`).
When an AOT method throws an exception that must be resumed in an interpreted catch
clause, the native unwinder transfers execution to the interpreter via
`interp_set_resume_state`.

Previously, `interp_set_resume_state` assumed that `context` was already initialized,
asserting `g_assert (context)` at interp.c:8299. For threads that have not previously
entered the interpreter, `context` is NULL, triggering an immediate assertion abort
and taking down the WebAssembly module.

This patch lazily initializes the thread's `InterpContext` via `get_context()`
in `interp_set_resume_state` when `context == NULL` prior to assigning the resume
frame and clause.
---
 src/mono/mono/mini/interp/interp.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/mono/mono/mini/interp/interp.c b/src/mono/mono/mini/interp/interp.c
index e5a4b3c2..8f7e6d5c 100644
--- a/src/mono/mono/mini/interp/interp.c
+++ b/src/mono/mono/mini/interp/interp.c
@@ -8295,8 +8295,15 @@ interp_set_resume_state (MonoInterpThreadState *state, InterpFrame *frame, Mono
 {
-	InterpContext *context = mono_tls_get_interp_context ();
-	g_assert (context);
+	InterpContext *context = mono_tls_get_interp_context ();
+
+	// ISSUE #138322: When resuming from WASM AOT-compiled code into an interpreted catch
+	// on a thread that has not yet entered the interpreter, context is NULL.
+	// Lazily initialize InterpContext via get_context() instead of asserting.
+	if (!context) {
+		context = get_context ();
+	}
+	g_assert (context);
 
 	context->resume_frame = frame;
 	context->resume_clause = clause;
 }
